Nets
Jen Bervin.
Author: 	Bervin, Jen.
Published: 	[S.l.] : Ugly Duckling Presse ;Berkeley : Distributed by Small Press Distribution, 2004.
Description: 	150 leaves ; 15 cm.
Format: 	Book
Summary:
Poetry. "Jen Bervin has reimagined Shakespeare as our true contemporary. Her little poems sing"--Paul Auster. In NETS, poet and artist Jen Bervin strips Shakespeare's sonnets "bare to the nets," chise ling away at the familiar lines to reveal surprising new poems, while pointing obliquely at the unavoidably intertextual ground of writing. Using visual compositional strategies as effectively as verbal ones, Bervin allows the discarded text to remain on the page as a ghostly presence, while she highlights the marginal line-numbers that allude to the sonnets' canonization.
